---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base
  title="Kalshi | Elisa Diop-Weyer"
  description="A startup idea for a meta-Kalshi, by emdw."
>
  <article class="essay-page">
    <a class="back-link" href={`${base}/musings/`}>← Selected Outputs</a>

    <header>
      <p class="tag">startup idea</p>
      <h1>Kalshi</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="essay-body">
      <p>Startup idea: a secondary Kalshi, a meta-Kalshi if you will, as in you can buy event contracts for the prices in the primary market. So you can exploit pricing deltas between the two markets. I think would be pretty fun arbitrage. Call it Lishak or Lakish or Alshik or something like that.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="signature">-- emdw 20261011</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .essay-page {
    width: min(100%, 48rem);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8em;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .back-link:hover,
  .back-link:focus-visible {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .tag {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8em;
    text-transform: lowercase;
  }

  h1 {
    font-style: italic;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .essay-body {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .essay-body p {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .signature {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    text-align: right;
  }
</style>
